  "final_answer": "**Cause:** `suggestions.ts` called `POST /api/recommend`, but the backend has never served that path. The only recommendation route is `POST /api/colleges/recommend`, defined in `python-backend/api/routes.py`. That mismatch is the 404.\n\nThere was a second bug behind it. The backend's `RecommendRequest` requires a top-level `student_profile` field. `suggestions.ts` was sending `{student_id, answers}` directly, so fixing only the URL would have swapped the 404 for a 422.\n\n**Fix:** In both calls in `suggestions.ts` (`generateSuggestedColleges` and `generateSuggestedCollegesFromAnswers`) I did two things:\n- Changed the URL to `/api/colleges/recommend`.\n- Wrapped the body as `{ student_profile: { student_id, answers } }`. This matches what `collegeApi.ts` already sends.\n\nI didn't add a second `/api/recommend` route on the backend, so there is still exactly one recommendation route. `tests/check_recommend.py` now passes. It only reads files as text, so I haven't tested against a running backend.\n\n**Files changed (1):**\n- `client/src/services/college/suggestions.ts`",
